# SETUP's Heli Setup page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigTradHeli4.cs (PLAN.md
# §13.6 rows 63 and 71).
#
# The claim: InitialSetup adds the page under Mandatory Hardware only for a traditional helicopter
# with every parameter in (InitialSetup.cs:184-187, `isHeli && gotAllParams`); ConfigTradHeli is
# commented out (:186) and never listed. SITL's bundled copter is a quad, so its Mandatory Hardware
# goes straight from the heading to Frame Type (:189), and the page object is never shown.
#
# What the page does for a heli - the eight servo rows bound to SERVOn_FUNCTION, _MIN, _MAX, _TRIM
# and _REVERSED; the Swashplate, Throttle, Governor and Misc tables filled from their lists, each
# row a label with the units and a combo or a number bound to the parameter; every control writing
# its own parameter; Deactivate emptying the tables - is proved by the unit tests in
# crates/mp-gui/src/config/trad_heli.rs, over a heli's parameters: there is no heli SITL here.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-heli.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 5
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
# The count passes before the last parameters land.
expect params.value.FRAME_CLASS 1

click tab-setup
expect setup.pages ~ ConfigMandatory,ConfigFrameClassType
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
expect setup.groups ~ Mandatory Hardware=ConfigFrameClassType,
expect config.heli.active false
expect config.heli.swash.rows 0
expect config.heli.throttle.rows 0
expect config.heli.message none
